The upgrade is divided into two distinct phases to ensure zero disruption to existing functionality:

Phase 1: Stabilize the Existing Codebase (Surgical bug fixes).

Phase 2: Cloud Ingestion Architecture (Database expansion, Core Services, and Route integration).

Cloud Ingestion Architecture Roadmap
Database Expansion: Introduce provider_hash_mappings (Rosetta Stone), async_ingestion_jobs (Ledger), and add encrypted token columns to users.

State Management Updates: Introduce distributed Redis locking (SETNX) to prevent concurrent duplicate cloud downloads, and polling keys (ingest:{job_id}:progress).

Background Workers: Utilize FastAPI BackgroundTasks to stream 5MB blocks from cloud providers directly to the local disk, committing to DB only upon successful stream completion.

Route Exposure: Expose the endpoints required by the React frontend to initiate and poll these background jobs.

