## Phase 3: FTP Bulk Ingestion (v4.0) — Server-to-Server Dropzone Watcher

This phase adds the third ingestion category: **s2s (server-to-server)** file drops via FTP. An `alpine-ftp-server` Docker container shares the `uploads-data` volume with the FastAPI container. A background daemon thread polls the FTP dropzone directory and automatically ingests completed files.

### Architectural Context — Ingestion Flow Categories

| Category | Label | Path | Implementation |
|----------|-------|------|----------------|
| Local HTTP upload | c2s | Client → Server | `file_services.py` (chunked upload protocol) |
| Cloud provider | c2s2s | Client → Google/Microsoft → Server | `gdrive_service.py`, `sharepoint_service.py` |
| **FTP drop** | **s2s** | **Server → Server** | **`ftp_watcher.py` (background daemon thread)** |

